{
  "comment": [
    "The client scenarios of the conformance runner pinned in the CI job conformance-client, and what the job expects of each.",
    "required and not_scored: the client scenarios each revision's requirement set lists as scored and as run but never scored. The job's first step reads both lists from the pinned runner and fails on any scenario the runner lists that is not named here, or named here and not listed, so every expectation below is written against scenarios the runner has.",
    "run: the scenarios the fixture runs one by one at that revision, in both profile modes. The extensions of authorization (other grants, DPoP) are not run; they stay in the expected-failure files of the requirement runs. A scenario the runner introduced in the draft revision is run only at 2026-07-28, since the runner skips it at an earlier one.",
    "checks: the check ids a passing run of the scenario must report, each with a SUCCESS. rows: check names that must be SUCCESS too (where one id has a row per method or per tool). Any FAILURE or WARNING fails the run. The ids are named per scenario, not per revision, so an id the runner reports only at 2026-07-28 is listed only for scenarios run at that revision alone (sep-837-application-type-present); for the others such an id is still judged by the rule that no check may fail. Ids that only inform are not listed.",
    "expected_to_fail: runs (scenario@revision, per profile mode) that cannot pass yet; one of them that passes fails the job, so the list is kept exact."
  ],
